 (343, 'Let us think and reflect – I (Extracts)', [
  'Extract 1: i. communication happens quickly but lacks depth ii. C. A is true, but R is false. iii. True iv. C. The Lasting Joy of Written Words',
  'Extract 2: i. She ardently supported his choice to live and work in Anand, though life there lacked even simple comforts – so she too valued the cause of serving farmers. ii. truly values iii. C. comforting (the extract shows her as encouraging, understanding and thoughtful; check with your teacher). iv. “I shouldered my responsibilities with poise”']),
 (344, 'Let us think and reflect – II (Answer the questions)', [
  '1. The ceremony in Delhi in 1999 where the President awarded him the Padma Vibhushan; Siddharth wore the medal and asked to keep it.',
  '2. He gave up other careers, lived a simple life in Anand and devoted his life to farmers; it transformed his life into one of service and great achievement (White Revolution).',
  '3. He chose to serve poor dairy farmers instead of a comfortable job or going abroad because he felt he could contribute more meaningfully to the nation – it shows patriotism, selflessness and sense of duty.',
  '4. To share his experiences, values and reasons for serving farmers, so that Siddharth (and children of his generation) would read it later and be inspired to work for the country and humanity.',
  '5. I agree. Life gives us talents and opportunities; wasting time and talents is wrong. We should use them to learn, help others and contribute to society.',
  '6. Selfless service brings real, lasting rewards and benefits millions (like the dairy cooperative); everyone should contribute to the common good in some way.',
  '7. Her ardent support gave him everlasting strength and helped him carry his responsibilities calmly. It shows that a true partnership means sharing goals and supporting each other’s choices.',
  '8. Because if you are honest to yourself, you will not deceive others; integrity guides all actions. Being honest with oneself makes honesty with others natural and easy.',
  '9. He says failure is not putting in our best effort and not contributing to the common good. This is important for young people because it makes them value effort and service over results and prizes.']),
