 (350, 'Let us speak', [
  'I. Nouns – stress on 1st syllable: PROduce, CONtract, PROject, CONtent, REfuse. Verbs – stress on 2nd: proDUCE, conTRACT, proJECT, conTENT, reFUSE.',
  'II. “zhuh” /ʒ/: measure, leisure, enclosure, exposure, seizure, composure. “shuh” /ʃ/: reassure, ensure, fissure, unsure.',
  'Chunking: Life is queer / with its twists and turns, // As every one of us / sometimes learns, // And many a fellow / turns about / when he might have won / had he stuck it out. // Don’t give up / though the pace seems slow— / you may succeed / with another blow. // Often the goal / is nearer than it seems / to a faint and faltering man. //']),
 (351, 'Let us write – Letter to grandparents', [
  'Gudur, 5 September 2026 | Dear Thatha and Ammamma, I hope you are both healthy and happy. I am writing to thank you for the valuable lessons you have taught me. Thatha, your stories of hard work in the fields taught me to respect farmers and never waste food. Ammamma, you always share food with neighbours and help anyone in need – that taught me kindness. Because of you, I help my classmates with lessons, take part in cleanliness drives and give my old books to juniors. I want to study well and serve society like you. I will visit you during Dasara holidays. | With love and respect, | Your grandson, Suresh']),
 (353, 'Let us explore – Financial literacy', [
  '1. Learning early builds good habits – e.g., saving ₹5 a day in a piggy bank helped me buy my own books.',
  '2. I would think about needs vs wants, future goals and emergencies – save a major part, spend a little on something useful.',
  '3. Make a list of needs, estimate costs, compare prices, keep a written budget, avoid waste and keep some money for emergencies.',
  '4. It helps everyone manage money wisely, avoid debt, save for the future and protect themselves from fraud.']),
